The code statements that lead to the bug are:
ring->prod_index = ring->c_index & DMA_C_INDEX_MASK;
while (drop--) { ... }
Reason:
The code does not increment ring->free_bds after fast-forwarding the write pointer, so free buffer descriptors are leaked. It also does not call netdev_tx_reset_queue after dropping packets, causing queue state inconsistency.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
ring->free_bds += drop;
netdev_tx_reset_queue(netdev_get_tx_queue(dev, ring->index));
Reason:
The first line restores the free buffer descriptor count, preventing the leak. The second line notifies the networking stack that all pending packets have been dropped, allowing proper queue management.

